# Dual Remote Push

Shared updates must land on **both** remotes:

- `github` → `https://github.com/bagzcode/bcip.git`
- `local` → `http://localhost:3020/git/BCIP/BCIP.git`

After any commit that should be shared (or when the user asks to push), run dual push:

```bash
pnpm push:all
# or: bash infrastructure/scripts/push-all.sh
# or: git push-all
```

Do not treat a single-remote push as complete. If one remote fails (for example local HTTP 500), still push the other and report both outcomes honestly. Never print credentials or tokens.
